{{also|Dunkel}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|tunkal|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|Germanic|dunkalaz|dark|lang=de}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|dʰengw-|to smoke, fume|lang=de}}. Cognate with {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|dunker||dark|lang=gml}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈdʊŋkl̩/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-dunkel.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|dunkler|dunkelsten}}

# [[dark]]
#: Im Winter wird es früher '''dunkel'''. &mdash; In the winter, it gets '''dark''' earlier.
#: Das '''[[dunkle]]''' Rot gefällt mir besser. &mdash; I like the '''dark''' red better.

